       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline, which is 200 mg/day for adults. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify going above that. At this dose, the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, hyponatremia, and seizures.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n1. **A typo or unit slip.** If you meant 200 mg, 100 mg, or 40 mg daily, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **A deliberate off-label dose.** If so, confirm that and I'll enter 400 mg once daily with a note such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max. Confirmed intentional by attending.\" Tell me if you want different wording. It may also trigger pharmacy review.\n3. **A titration plan.** For example, 50 mg daily, increasing by 50 mg at weekly intervals to a target. I can enter the starting dose and note the plan.\n\nLet me know which one and I'll enter it."
      }
